\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ b & c & a \\ c & a & b \end{vmatrix} &= a \begin{vmatrix} c & a \\ a & b \end{vmatrix} - b \begin{vmatrix} b & a \\ c & b \end{vmatrix} + c \begin{vmatrix} b & c \\ c & a \end{vmatrix} \\
&= a(bc - a^2) - b(b^2 - ac) + c(ab - c^2) \\
&= -a^3 -b^2 - c^2 + 3abc.
\end{align*}When this matrix is not invertible, we have $-a^3 - b^2 - c^2 + 3abc = 0,$ or $a^3 + b^2 + c^2 = 3abc.$

Dividing both sides by $abc,$ we get
\[\frac{a^2}{bc} + \frac{b}{ac} + \frac{c}{ab} = 3.\]Then
\[\frac{a}{b + c} + \frac{b}{a + c} + \frac{c}{a + b} = \frac{3}{2}.\][asy]
